ther Habsburg lands lay outside the Empire, so the Habsburg Monarchy is not merged into it on the map.","The Duchy of Prussia lay outside the Empire, so Brandenburg-Prussia is not merged into it on the map.","After the death of Möngke Khan (1259) the empire split into four khanates that still nominally recognised the Great Khan until 1294. Cliopatria draws one Mongol Empire until 1293, so they are listed here but not drawn apart.","The kings of Spain were also kings of Portugal from 1580 to 1640; Portugal and its colonies (Brazil, Goa, Angola) kept their own administration. Cliopatria draws them inside the Spanish Empire in these years.","Ceded by France in 1762 and returned in 1800; Cliopatria leaves it blank.","CShapes draws the Soviet Union as one state; its republics are listed but not drawn apart.","A puppet state set up by Japan in Manchuria; CShapes draws the area as part of China.","CShapes 2.0 has no outline for Greenland in these years, so it is listed here but not drawn."],"stats":{"memberships":424,"verified":216,"drawn":353,"listedOnly":71,"bySource":{"cliopatria":[148,93],"curatedOwners":[158,49],"sketchMaps":[12,4],"curatedEmpires":[106,70]},"empires":34}}